EXTENDS Naturals, FiniteSets, TLC
CONSTANTS Nodes, Values
VARIABLES state, votes, decision
TypeOK ==
/\ state \in [Nodes -> {"proposing", "voting", "decided"}]
/\ votes \in [Nodes -> Values \cup {"NoVote"}]
/\ decision \in Values \cup {"NoDecision"}
Init ==
/\ state = [n \in Nodes |-> "proposing"]
/\ votes = [n \in Nodes |-> "NoVote"]
/\ decision = "NoDecision"
Propose(n, v) ==
/\ state[n] = "proposing"
/\ state' = [state EXCEPT ![n] = "voting"]
/\ votes' = [votes EXCEPT ![n] = v]
/\ UNCHANGED <<decision>>
Decide(v) ==
/\ \exists S \subseteq Nodes:
/\ Cardinality(S) * 2 > Cardinality(Nodes)
/\ \forall n \in S: votes[n] = v
/\ decision' = v
/\ state' = [n \in Nodes |-> "decided"]
/\ UNCHANGED <<votes>>
Next ==
/ \exists n \in Nodes, v \in Values: Propose(n,v)
/ \exists v \in Values: Decide(v)
Spec == Init /\ [][Next]_<<state, votes, decision>>
* Safety: No two different values are decided.
Agreement ==
[](\A v1, v2 \in Values:
(decision = v1 /\ decision = v2) => v1 = v2)
* Validity: If a value is decided, it must have been proposed by at least one node. Validity == [](decision \in Values => \exists n \in Nodes: votes[n] = decision)
